ZTEXT00100000e4f1d5dedd70000000
Zero BIOS true-color graphics

bios.zero selects a linear VBE2/3 framebuffer before entering the kernel.
The implementation is Zero source. The compiler provides only the firmware
INT10 ABI operation :vbe[ax|bx|cx|buffer] and the real-mode segment access
:far16[segment|offset]; mode discovery, validation, selection, page tables
and loader handoff are all expressed by bios.zero.

The VBE controller query uses a zeroed 512-byte buffer at6200 with the VBE2
request signature. A VESA response and VBE version>=0200 are required. The
actual firmware-provided far mode list is examined, at most256 entries per
pass. Three passes prefer1920x1080, then800x600, then640..800 by480..600
when the larger modes are unavailable or fail to set. Every mode candidate
still undergoes the same format, stride, memory-size and address checks.
A list terminator, segment-offset overflow or address beyond the first MiB
stops discovery. far16 permits reading a list in firmware ROM without
violating the real-mode DS=0 64KiB segment limit.

Each mode query uses a separate zeroed256-byte buffer at6400. Eligible modes
are supported graphics modes with a linear framebuffer, one plane,32 bits
per pixel and direct-color memory model6. The first pass accepts only
1920x1080, the second only800x600, and the last the smaller fallback range.
FullHD requires at least8294400 framebuffer bytes at a1920-pixel stride.
Pitch must cover width*4, be a multiple of4 and
be at most16384 bytes. Frame size must fit reported video memory; the physical
base must be at least4MiB, beyond the owned stack pool, and the entire extent
must not wrap32-bit arithmetic.

Red, green and blue masks must each have8bits. Green must start at bit8;
red/blue must occupy bits0/16 or16/0. Thus the kernel receives format0RGB or
format1BGR, using4bytes per pixel. The high reserved byte is not an alpha API.
VBE3 uses the linear pitch and linear color-mask fields; VBE2 uses its legacy
mode fields. The first eligible mode whose SetMode succeeds is selected,
with the linear-framebuffer flag. If no mode succeeds, BIOS text mode3 is
restored and the existing VGA text handoff is retained.

Shared handoff
+48 kind2 for a selected framebuffer, otherwise kind1 VGA text
+56 physical framebuffer base
+64 width, +72 height, +80 stride in pixels, +88 format0RGB/1BGR
+96 bootkind1, +104 architecture32 or64
+112 stack pool physical base100000, +120 pool bytes300000
All fields are u64; BIOS clears128bytes first and fills low halves with u32.
The main kernel entry stack starts at400000. The complete1..4MiB pool must be
usable E820 RAM, as documented in BIOS.ztext; this is not a general RAM allocator.

BIOS64 identity-maps the entire first4GiB using2MiB pages. PML4 is1000,
PDPT2000 and the four page directories are3000,4000,5000,c000. Every page-table
store is below the64KiB real-mode segment limit. The loader never calls reserve,
so4000..5fff can hold two directories; c000 follows the maximum BIOS image
extent7c00..bbff. The disk DAP at3900 is reused only after all disk reads finish.
VBE buffers6200/6400, E820 buffer6600, ABI scratch6e00, locals6f00, stack below7c00,
GDT0800 and handoff0900 remain separate. The temporary E820 interval bank at
4000..47ff is no longer needed when page tables are built. BIOS32 uses flat
segments with paging disabled,
so it can address the same32-bit physical framebuffer directly.

There is no universal video-device claim. Unsupported bit-mask formats,
24-bit modes, banked modes and incompatible firmware retain the text path.
See verification/bios-graphics-0.6.0/ for isolated pixel/firmware probes and
verification.ztext for the final integrated release checks.
